Albra Serif Font/

# Catalogue PDFs mirrored from sarom.info — ~660MB across 204 files.
# Deliberately NOT tracked: a repo that size is painful to clone, and they are
# already hosted. reference/catalogue-manifest.json IS committed, so the set
# rebuilds with `node reference/fetch-pdfs.mjs`.
# Scoped to *.pdf, NOT the whole folder: the cover images live alongside them
# and are only ~6MB, and the showroom renders blank without them.
#
# Since 2026-10-14 ALL 229 are SERVED from the VPS, not from this repo or
# sarom.info: https://sarom.co.in/catalogues/... -> /var/www/sarom.co.in/catalogues
# (same folder layout as here). `pdf` in lib/catalogues.ts points there. To add or
# replace a catalogue: put the file here, then stream the folder up with
#   tar -cf - <pdfs> | ssh root@187.126.125.131 'tar -xf - -C /var/www/sarom.co.in/catalogues'
# 26 of them (the client's "PDF - Website" drop) exist nowhere else but the
# server, this machine and the client's zip — sarom.info never had them.
public/catalogues/**/*.pdf

.vercel

# Env files. Nothing uses them today, but `vercel` offers to write .env.local
# during setup and this repo is public — a committed key is a leaked key.
.env
.env*.local

# ---- Client source deliveries, dropped straight into the repo root ----
# ~18.6GB: WeTransfer archives plus the loose CMYK print originals they were
# unpacked from (one TIFF is 849MB, one zip 5.3GB). The web covers BUILT from
# them are tracked under public/catalogues/_covers; these masters are not, for
# the same reason the catalogue PDFs above are not.
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. That is the whole point:
# a bare `*.tif` or `*.png` would also swallow public/ and reference/, and the
# covers are the deliverable. Verified before adding — zero tracked files sit
# at the repo root with these extensions.
/*.tif
/*.tiff
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.zip
/PDF - Website/
